# Syntax: docs/LANGUAGE.md. Check with `rbb bid check`.
#
# The Impossible 2♠ (Robert Todd, "The Impossible ♠ Bid", Adventures in
# Bridge TWiB 269; GIB's "Impossible spade"): after 1♥–1NT, responder has
# denied four spades, so a later 2♠ over opener's 2♣ or 2♦ cannot be
# natural. It shows a good raise of opener's minor: four or more, the top
# of the 1NT response, and forcing to three of the minor. The plain raise
# to 3m stays the lesser raise (responder-rebids.bid). Only after a 1♥
# opening (over 1♠, 2♠ is a preference) and only over a minor rebid: our
# 1NT denies three hearts, so Todd's 1♥–1NT–2♥–2♠ (a three-card limit
# raise) has no hand here. See impossible-2s.notes.md.

module impossible-2s "Impossible 2♠"
  card   major_openings.impossible_2s.play
  needs  responder-rebids
  skill  bidding_conventions/impossible_2s

# ── Responder: the good raise ────────────────────────────────────────
# Our 1NT is 6-10 HCP, so the raise to 3m (9-10 points) is the courtesy
# raise and 2♠ takes the 11+ hands (10 HCP and a fifth trump, or a
# sixth), which had no call at all and passed.
after 1H (P) 1N (P) 2m (P)
  2S  "Impossible 2♠: good raise of {m}, 4+ {m}, 11+ points"  alert
      shows m>=4, H<=2, points>=11
      sets  trump=m, forcing=round
      artificial

# ── Opener answers ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Responder has 11-13 with the fit, so opener goes to game with 15+
# support points (HCP and shortness: a 5-4-3-1 twelve-count, a 5-4-2-2
# thirteen; GIB's minimum is 12-13 total points): 3NT with both unbid suits stopped, otherwise the
# stopper he has (up the line, looking for 3NT, with the minor as the
# fallback; responder answers in responder-rebids.bid), otherwise five
# of the minor. With a minimum he signs off in three of the minor.
after 1H (P) 1N (P) 2C (P) 2S (P)
  3C  "Minimum: no game opposite the good raise"
      shows tp(C)<=14
      sets  ask=signoff
  3N  "Game: 15+, spades and diamonds stopped"
      shows tp(C)>=15, stop(S), stop(D)
  3D  "Diamond stopper, not spades: looking for 3NT"
      shows tp(C)>=15, stop(D), !stop(S)
      sets  ask=stoppers, ladder=stopper, forcing=game
  3S  "Spade stopper, not diamonds: looking for 3NT"
      shows tp(C)>=15, stop(S), !stop(D)
      sets  ask=stoppers, ladder=stopper, forcing=game
  5C  "Game in clubs: 15+, neither suit stopped"
      shows tp(C)>=15
      priority -1
after 1H (P) 1N (P) 2D (P) 2S (P)
  3D  "Minimum: no game opposite the good raise"
      shows tp(D)<=14
      sets  ask=signoff
  3N  "Game: 15+, spades and clubs stopped"
      shows tp(D)>=15, stop(S), stop(C)
  3C  "Club stopper, not spades: looking for 3NT"
      shows tp(D)>=15, stop(C), !stop(S)
      sets  ask=stoppers, ladder=stopper, forcing=game
  3S  "Spade stopper, not clubs: looking for 3NT"
      shows tp(D)>=15, stop(S), !stop(C)
      sets  ask=stoppers, ladder=stopper, forcing=game
  5D  "Game in diamonds: 15+, neither suit stopped"
      shows tp(D)>=15
      priority -1

# ── Responder after opener's minimum ─────────────────────────────────
after 1H (P) 1N (P) 2m (P) 2S (P) 3m (P)
  P   "Opener is minimum: play three of {m}"

# ── Responder after opener's game ────────────────────────────────────
after 1H (P) 1N (P) 2m (P) 2S (P) 3N (P) | 1H (P) 1N (P) 2m (P) 2S (P) 5m (P)
  P   "Opener has placed the contract"
